"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record for Ransom County runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids June to July is the wettest pair at 6.68 inches of normal. February to March and October to November each came in under 90% of normal in 40 of those years. On the middle of the grids, 2026 so far ran 67% of normal in March to April and 67% in June to July, after 2025 hit 134% in August to September. Grid 31631 had its driest year in 1976 at 37%.</p>"}
